\pt0.42;{\fArial Narrow|b0|i0|c0|p34;\C1;(1)	\LHYDRANT SYSTEM :-\C256;\P\ptz;\l\C7;	ON/OFF SWITCHES LOCATED NEAR THE  HOSE REEL HOSE OR HYDRANT OUTLET, AT EACH FLOOR FOR THE MAIN FIRE-PUMP AT UNDERGROUND WATER TANK WITH A CAPACITY TO DISCHARGE 900 LI
  3
TERS PER MINUTE AT 3 BAR PRESSURE AS MEASURED AT THE TERRACE LEVEL SHOULD BE INSTALLED. \P	THE RISER FOR THE BUILDINGS EXCEEDING 18 MITERS HEIGHT SHOULD NOT BE OF LESS THAN 100 MM. INTERNAL DIAMETER. THE RISER SHOULD BE CONNECTED TO THE BOTTOM OF THE
  3
 TERRACE TANK WITH A STOP VALVE AND A NRV TO ACT A DOWN-COMER.\P	ONE RISER IS REQUIRED FOR EVERY 1000 SQ. METERS FLOOR AREA AND IF THE BUILDING IS DIVIDED INTO, TWO OR MORE PARTS THEN EACH PART SHOULD HAVE A SEPARATE RISER WITH ALL THE FITTINGS AT EA
  3
CH FLOOR LEVEL.\P	EACH FLOOR SHOULD HAVE ONE HYDRANT OUTLET WITH A COUPLING FOR ATTACHING A 63 MM. DIA . HOSE . 25 MM. BORE HOSE- REEL HOSE WITH 8 MM. SHUT- OFF NOZZLE AT EACH FLOOR LANDING. THE LENGTH OF THE HOSE SHOULD BE ENOUGH TO REACH THE FARTHE
  3
ST CORNER OR THE FLOOR. HOSE-BOX WITH\P15 METERS LONG 63 MM.  DIA. HOSE AND 12.5 MM. BORE NOZZLE AT ALTERNATE FLOORS. THE HOSE-REEL HOSE SHOULD BE COUPLED TO THE RISER.\P	FIRE - SERVICE INLET SHOULD BE  INSTALLED AT A POINT NEAR THE ENTRY TO THE PERM
  3
ISES WHERE A FIRE SERVICE VEHICLE CAN APPROACH EASILY.\P	A PERMANENT HYDRANT POINT COMPRISING OF 63 MM DIA SIZE 2 NOS OF HYDRANT VALVES SHOULD BE INSTALLED AT THE TERRACE LEVEL.\P	OVERHEAD TANK REFILLING BYPASS CONNECTION SHOULD BE DONE AT THE TERRAC
  3
E LEVEL.\P	THE OVERHEAD TANK SHALL BE OF A CAPACITY OF NOT LESS THAN 20,000 LITERS. THE UNDERGROUND TANK SHALL BE OF NOT LESS THAN 1,00,000 LITERS.\C1;\P\pt0.42;(2)	\LFIRE LIFT :-\C256;\P\ptz;\l	\C7;THE FIRE-LIFT AND ALL LIFTS SHOULD HAVE A PROVISION
  3
 TO GROUND TO AUTOMATICALLY IN CASE OF ELECTRICITY FAILURE . EACH BUILDING SHOULD HAVE AT LEAST ONE LIFT AS A FIRE -LIFT AND IF THE BUILDING IS DIVIDED INTO A MORE PARTS THEN  EACH PART SHOULD HAVE A FIRE-LIFT. LIFT-WELL SHOULD HAVE BLOWERS TO PRESSU
  3
RIZE THE LIFT -WELL SO CONNECTED THAT IT WILL AUTOMATICALLY OPERATE WHEN ALARM CALL POINT IS OPERATE, SO THAT IF PREVENTS THE LIFT WELL GETTING SMOKE LOGGED.\P\L\C1;(3) FIRE ALARM :-\C256;\P\l	\C7;FIRE ALARM CALL POINT TO BE INSTALLED AT EACH FLOOR W
  3
ITH SOUNDERS CAPABLE OF BEING HEARD ALL THROUGHOUT THE BUILDING\C0;.\P\L\C1;(4) FIRE EXTINGUISHERS :-\C256;\P\l	\C7;ONE CARBON DIOXIDE (CO2 ) TYPE EXTINGUISHER OF 4.5 KG. WITH ISI MARK. AND ONE EXTINGUISHER OF 5 KG. DRY CHEMICAL POWDER (DCP) TYPE EXT
  3
INGUISHER WITH ISI MARK TO INSTALLED ON EACH FLOOR IN CASE OF COMMERCIAL BUILDING.\P	ONE CARBON DIOXIDE (CO2 ) TYPE EXTINGUISHER OF 4.5 KG. WITH ISI MARK. OR TWO CARBON DIOXIDE (CO2 ) TYPE EXTINGUISHER OF 2 KG. CAPACITY ON EACH FLOOR AND 5 KG. DRY CH
  3
EMICAL POWDER (DCP) WITH ISI MARK TYPE EXTINGUISHER ON ALTERNATE FLOOR IN CASE OF RESIDENTIAL BUILDINGS.\P	IF THE BUILDING IS DIVIDED INTO TWO OR MORE PARTS THEN EACH PART SHOULD HAVE THESE EXTINGUISHERS INSTALLED.\C256;\P\C1;(5) \LSTAIRCASE :-\C256;
  3
\P\l	\C7;THE STAIRCASE HAS TO BE OPEN FROM AT LEAST ONE OR TWO SIDES BUT IF THE STAIRCASE IS IN THE CENTRE CORE OF THE BUILDING IT HAS TO BE PRESSURIZED TO PREVENT IT FROM GETTING SMOKE LOGGED.\P	THE  RISER / DOWN - COMER SHOULD BE LOCATED IN THE STA
  3
IRCASE OR CLOSE TO IN TO MAKE IT EASILY APPROACHABLE IN CASE OF FIRE FROM THE FLOOR BELOW OR ABOVE\C256;.\P\L\C1;(6) BASEMENT :-\C256;\P\l	\C7;THE BASEMENT OF 200 SQ. METERS OR MORE SHOULD BE  PROTECTED WITH AUTOMATIC SPRINKLER SYSTEM WITH AT LEAST O
  3
NE SPRINKLE HEAD FOR ACTUAL CAR PARKING SPACE.\P	ADDITIONALLY BE PROTECTED BY A HYDRANT OUTLET AND TWO 25 MM. BORE HOSE- REEL HOSES  WITH 8MM . BORE  NOZZLES AT EACH BASEMENT LEVEL.\P\C1;(7)\L LIGHTENING ARRESTER :-\C256;\P\l\C7;	A LIGHTENING ARRESTE
  3
R SHOULD ALSO BE INSTALLED AND BE PROPERLY EARTHED TO PREVENT DAMAGE TO THE BUILDING WHEN THE LIGHTENING STRIKES.\P\C1;(8) \LPHOTO LUMINESCENT ( AUTO GLOW ) SIGNAGE'S :\l\C256;\P\C7;	IF THE BUILDING FALLS IN A CONFINED AREA OR IF IT HAS AN ENCLOSED S
  3
TAIRCASE OR IS NOT WELL LIT-UP ON THE INSIDE, THEN ADEQUATE PHOTO LUMINESCENT ( AUTO GLOW ) SIGNAGE'S SHOULD BE DISPLAYED AT EACH FLOOR / LANDING / PATHWY / DEAD-END AND ALONG ALL EXIT ROUTES LANDING TO THE GROUND LEVEL. THE SIGNAGE SHOULD INDICATE F
  3
IRE FIGHTING, FIRE SAFETY, FIRST-AID AND OTHER SAFETY EQUIPEMENT PRESENT ON THE RESPECTIVE FLOOR / LANDING / PATHWAY / DEAD - END AND ALONG ALL EXIT ROUTES LEADING TO THE GROUND LEVEL.\P\C1;(9) \LELECTRIC POWER SUPPLY TO THE ENTIRE FIRE - SAFETY SYST
  3
EM :-\C256;\P\l\C7;	ELECTRICITY SUPPLY TO THE FIRE PUMP, FIRE ALARM SYSTEM, STAIRCASE PRESSURIZATION SYSTEM AND FIRE LIFT SHOULD BE MADE AVAILABLE FROM THE MAIN ELECTRICAL SUPPLY. ( I.E. FROM ELECTRICAL POWER SUPPLY OF THE COMPANY ) THIS IS TO ENSURE
  3
 AVAILABILITY OF POWER SUPPLY TO THE FIRE PROTECTION & SAFETY SYSTEM EVEN AFTER THE MAIN ELECTRICAL SUPPLY TO THE BUILDING IS SWITCHED OFF THE TIME OF FIRE.\P\L\C1;(10) IMPORTANT INSTRUCTIONS :-\C256;\P\l\C7;	AFTER INSPECTION OF A LOW-RISE BUILDING B
  3
Y THE FIRE SERVICES AUTHORITY , IF THE FIRE OFFICER CONCERNED FEELS THE NEED FOR ADDITIONAL FIRE PREVENTION / PROTECTION / VENTILATION SYSTEM REQUIRED OR EQUIPEMENT ( I.E. PASSIVE SYSTEM / SPRIKLER / DRENCHER ETC. ) AS PER FIRE LOAD / FIRE RISK / PUB
  1
LIC GETHERING. POTENTIAL / OCCUPANCY / CONFINED AREA, THOSE ADDITIONAL MEASURES / EQUIPEMENT HAVE TO BE\C256; \C7;IMPLEMENTED / INSTALLED.}
  7
